  "id": "counterfactual-thinking",
  "term": "counterfactual thinking",
  "definition": "Counterfactual thinking is the mental ability to imagine how events could have happened differently from what actually occurred. It helps regulate emotions and behavior, and problems with it may make it harder to adjust actions and feelings.",
